# Suggestion Triage

Read `.cursor/skills/suggestion-triage.md` before triaging suggestions or running the automation. Each run does two jobs in order: **maintain** the existing `suggestion` issues, then **discover** new ones.

Key points:
- **Ownership boundary (hard rule):** only ever close / relabel / edit / comment-to-close issues that carry the `suggestion` label — the ones this flow owns. Every other issue (backlog units, epics, human-filed) is READ-ONLY. Run the pre-write label gate (`gh issue view N --json labels`) before any write.
- **Maintenance first:** close suggestions the code/spec *proves* resolved or obsolete, mark + link duplicates, refresh drifted bodies, and add `stale` (don't close) when you can't prove resolution. Close only what you can cite.
- **Read-only on code** — this flow files/maintains GitHub issues only. Never edit files, push branches, or open PRs.
- **Net-growth budget:** prefer refreshing a near-match over filing new; cap net-new per run (tighter when the open `suggestion` backlog is large); a run that nets negative is a success. Filing **zero** new issues is valid; never pad. Keep at most ~2 findings from recently-changed files.
- Every new issue gets `suggestion` + one `area:<x>` + one `severity:<x>` label, the standard body template, and a hidden fingerprint marker. Dedup: search open and closed `label:suggestion` for `fp=<area>/<slug>` (no line number) and skip/refresh if it exists.
- The dashboard automation config (triggers, model, `GITHUB_PAT` secret, settings) lives in `docs/internal/ci-cd/CURSOR_AUTOMATIONS.md`. Issues are created/searched via `gh` CLI (`export GH_TOKEN="$GITHUB_PAT"`) — no MCP server needed.
